GNU datetime NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

* Version 2.0.20260913 (2026-09-13)

** Changes in behavior

  `datetime -d ''` (empty or whitespace-only date string) now matches GNU
  date: today at midnight, instead of an error.
  `datetime -Ins` / `--iso-8601=auto` prints a dot as the ISO 8601 decimal
  separator where GNU date prints a comma (documented deviation).

** Tests

  New differential suite `tests/_test_matrix` (267 cases) compares every
  option and an option-combination matrix against the installed GNU date,
  and caught three bugs on the way in: `-d 20200102` was shadowed by the
  MMDDhhmm set-time path, ISO dates with an explicit `+02:00` offset
  ignored the zone, and `-d ''` errored instead of meaning today.
  New root runner `./_tests [--details]` executes every suite in `tests/`
  (per-case parameters and results with green OK / red FAILED under
  --details); `make check` runs it and CI executes the matrix suite.

  The separate `timestamp` binary is gone.  `datetime --timestamp` selects the
  UTC `YYYYMMDDhhmmssZ` format at run time, per GNU Coding Standards section
  17 (behavior must not depend on the name used to invoke the program).

** Bug fixes

  `datetime -d 09:00` (bare time-only date) no longer reports year 1899;
  it is anchored on today's date like GNU date.
  `datetime -r FILE` no longer loses sub-second precision; nanoseconds from
  the file's mtime are printed with %N again (the `#if defined(st_mtim)`
  check was always false because st_mtim is a struct field, not a macro).

** Simplifications

  The generated `version.h` header is gone; the build number is passed with
  `-DVERSION_BUILD` from the Makefile.  format_time handles %N/%q/%s/%z and
  the %:z family through a table instead of duplicated special cases, with a
  single bounds-checked append helper.  main() delegates operand scanning to
  scan_operand and MMDDhhmm set-time parsing to parse_mmddhhmm.

* Version 2.0 (2026-09-09)

** Optimizations and performance

  Single-pass format_time engine replaces intermediate 8KB buffer transformations,
  emitting directly to destination and eliminating 16 KB of stack allocation.
  Zero format-truncation compiler warnings.

** Robustness and bug fixes

  Fixed negative epoch nanosecond calculation for fractional timestamps (@-1, @-0.5).
  Centralized resource cleanup via goto cleanup in main(), guaranteeing 0 memory leaks.
  Deduplicated legacy format handlers and day offset parsers (today/yesterday/tomorrow).

** Cross-platform portability

  Windows (MinGW-w64/MSYS2): Added timezone shims (_tzset, _get_timezone, _daylight,
  _tzname) when tm_gmtoff/tm_zone are absent in struct tm.
  macOS (Darwin): Added st_mtimespec support for sub-second file modification timestamps.
  Valgrind check gracefully skips when unavailable on macOS.

** Test suite & Verification

  Makefile check target now runs check-syntax, check-mem (valgrind), check-style
  (indent -gnu), and check-test (406 bash tests + 40 pytest tests / 244 subtests).

* Version 1.3 (2026-09-09)

** New GNU date compatible options (see date_english.hlp)

  -d, --date=STRING          display time described by STRING, not `now'
      --debug                annotate parsed date, warn to stderr
  -f, --file=DATEFILE        file input, - for stdin
  -I[FMT], --iso-8601[=FMT]   date/hours/minutes/seconds/ns
      --resolution           0.000000001
  -R, --rfc-email            RFC 5322
      --rfc-3339=FMT         date/seconds/ns
  -r, --reference=FILE       file mtime
  -s, --set=STRING           set system time (needs root)
  -u, --utc, --universal     UTC
  +FORMAT                    full GNU date FORMAT with 47 sequences

  All mutually exclusive options enforced (--date/--file/--reference/--resolution).
  FORMAT supports flags -_0+^#, width, E/O modifiers, %N nanoseconds, %q quarter,
  %z/%:z/%::z/%:::z timezones.

** Strict GNU compliance

  Makefile now has SHELL, prefix/bindir/mandir, INSTALL_PROGRAM, distclean/TAGS/dist,
  version.h uses robust BUILD fallback, datetime.c uses getopt_long, braces in column
  zero, dynamic allocation (no 4096 limits), no argv[0] dispatch (use --timestamp or
  -DTIMESTAMP), Texinfo manual and man page added.

** Build

  C99 strict (gcc -std=c99), only libc.  `make` now builds and installs to ~/sbin
  (or $(bindir)), `make check` runs valgrind, 650+ tests (406 bash + 244 Python subtests).

** Documentation

  README: C99 note, Index, extensive Example usage (50+), Timestamp microversion docs
  (1.3.<build> = 1.3.20260909083730Z).  date_english.hlp regenerated, ESC-free.
  New man/man1/datetime.1 and tldr/datetime.md, manual.texi, ChangeLog.

** Fixes

  ESC sequences filtered from date_german.hlp (72 -> 0).  Robust BUILD fallback for
  clean systems.  Shell injection blocked via shell_escape, 8192 bounds via malloc.
  Tests fixed for 1.3 version string.

* Version 1.2 (2026-09-05)

  Legacy formats: -hr/--human-readable, -c/--compact/iso-basic, -cd/--calendar-date,
  -cdb/--calendar-date-base, -od/--ordinal-date, -odb/--ordinal-date-base,
  -wd/--week-date, -wdb/--week-date-basic, --timestamp.  Initial timestamp utility.

* Version 1.0 (2026-09-05)

  Initial import.  Prints local YYYYMMDDhhmmss, human-readable, basic ISO.
